  "name": "@lightsage/mcp-tracker",
  "readme": "# @lightsage/mcp-tracker\n\nTrack MCP tool calls from AI agents. Works with `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, FastMCP, and custom servers.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @lightsage/mcp-tracker\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### AI Wizard\n\nThe fastest way to get set up:\n\n```bash\nnpx @lightsage/wizard mcp-analytics\n```\n\n### MCP SDK (Low-level Server)\n\n```typescript\nimport { Server } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/index.js\";\nimport { Lightsage } from \"@lightsage/mcp-tracker\";\n\nconst server = new Server({ name: \"my-mcp-server\", version: \"1.0.0\" });\n\nconst lightsage = new Lightsage(\"sap_your_api_key\");\nconst analytics = lightsage.instrument(server);\n\n// Register your tools as usual...\n```\n\n### McpServer (High-level Wrapper)\n\n```typescript\nimport { McpServer } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/mcp.js\";\nimport { Lightsage } from \"@lightsage/mcp-tracker\";\n\nconst server = new McpServer({ name: \"my-mcp-server\", version: \"1.0.0\" });\n\nconst lightsage = new Lightsage(\"sap_your_api_key\");\nlightsage.instrument(server);\n\n// Tools registered after instrument() are also tracked\nserver.tool(\"search_docs\", { query: z.string() }, async ({ query }) => {\n  return { content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"Results...\" }] };\n});\n```\n\n### Next.js (mcp-handler)\n\n```typescript\nimport { createMcpHandler } from \"mcp-handler\";\nimport { Lightsage } from \"@lightsage/mcp-tracker\";\n\nconst lightsage = new Lightsage(process.env.LIGHTSAGE_API_KEY);\n\nconst handler = createMcpHandler(\n  (server) => {\n    lightsage.instrument(server);\n    server.tool(\"search_docs\", { query: z.string() }, async ({ query }) => {\n      return { content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"Results...\" }] };\n    });\n  },\n  {},\n  { basePath: \"/api/mcp\" }\n);\n\nexport { handler as GET, handler as POST };\n```\n\n### NestJS (@rekog/mcp-nest)\n\n```typescript\nimport { Module } from \"@nestjs/common\";\nimport { McpModule } from \"@rekog/mcp-nest\";\nimport { Lightsage, instrumentMutator } from \"@lightsage/mcp-tracker\";\n\nconst lightsage = new Lightsage(process.env.LIGHTSAGE_API_KEY);\n\n@Module({\n  imports: [\n    McpModule.forRoot({\n      name: \"my-mcp-server\",\n      version: \"1.0.0\",\n      serverMutator: instrumentMutator(lightsage),\n    }),\n  ],\n})\nexport class AppModule {}\n```\n\n### Custom Server (No MCP SDK)\n\n```typescript\nimport { LightsageMCP } from \"@lightsage/mcp-tracker\";\n\nconst lightsage = new LightsageMCP(\"sap_your_api_key\");\n\n// Manually capture tool calls\nlightsage.captureToolCall({\n  toolName: \"search_docs\",\n  parameters: { query: \"authentication\" },\n  response: { content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"...\" }] },\n  durationMs: 142,\n  isError: false,\n  distinctId: \"user_123\",\n  sessionId: \"session_abc\",\n});\n\n// Capture the initialize handshake\nlightsage.captureInitialize({\n  clientName: \"claude-code\",\n  clientVersion: \"1.2.3\",\n  distinctId: \"user_123\",\n});\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n```typescript\nconst lightsage = new Lightsage({\n  apiKey: \"sap_...\",\n  endpoint: \"https://ls.lightsage.com/api/v1/mcp-analytics/track\", // optional\n  enableExceptionAutocapture: true, // default: true\n  enableContext: true, // inject context argument for intent capture\n  enableConversationId: false, // inject conversation_id argument\n  reportMissing: false, // register get_more_tools virtual tool\n});\n```\n\n### Environment Variables\n\n```bash\nLIGHTSAGE_API_KEY=sap_...\n# or\nLIGHTSAGE_MCP_KEY=sap_...\n```\n\n## What Gets Tracked\n\n| Event | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `$mcp_tool_call` | Tool name, arguments, result, latency, errors |\n| `$mcp_initialize` | Client name, version, session start |\n| `$mcp_tools_list` | Discovery events, available tools |\n| `$exception` | Auto-captured errors with stack traces |\n| `$mcp_missing_capability` | Tools agents asked for that don't exist |\n\n### Tool Call Event\n\n```typescript\ninterface ToolCallEvent {\n  toolName: string;\n  toolDescription?: string;\n  parameters?: Record<string, unknown>;\n  response?: unknown;\n  durationMs: number;\n  isError: boolean;\n  errorMessage?: string;\n  errorType?: string;\n  distinctId?: string;\n  sessionId?: string;\n  clientName?: string;\n  clientVersion?: string;\n  intent?: string;\n  conversationId?: string;\n}\n```\n\n## Graceful Shutdown\n\n```typescript\nprocess.on(\"SIGTERM\", async () => {\n  await lightsage.flush();\n  lightsage.shutdown();\n  process.exit(0);\n});\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
